WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Run every scenario action, inspect the Java implementation, and verify each change inside Oracle AI Database.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The library stores preference, fact, guideline, and memory records. Message represents recent conversation from a separate table.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The library panels become empty. The lifecycle path retains only the Ava and Leo visitor identities.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The Java library clears persisted messages and extracted records, then clears the in-process search result and context-card view.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Oracle AI Database deletes OAMJ_CONCIERGE_MESSAGE and OAMJ_CONCIERGE_RECORDS rows. Red rows show what was removed.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Java deletes mutable teaching records in foreign-key-safe order and preserves the two visitor identities used by both application lanes.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The AIM_DEMO tables are empty except for Ava and Leo in AIM_DEMO_GUESTS. Browser state is not carrying memory.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:03.000
The app shows two current messages, extracted records, and one seeded prior-visit memory inserted by addMemory().

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Ollama classifies durable content and Oracle AI Database creates an ALLMINILM embedding for every stored record.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.000
OAMJ_CONCIERGE_MESSAGE stores the conversation. OAMJ_CONCIERGE_RECORDS stores typed, identity-scoped records with native vectors.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:27.000
The UI exposes type, scope, source, version, status, and expiration so the broader lifecycle is easy to explain.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Java inserts four durable Ava memories, one temporary route fact, and three de-identified successful traces.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:43.000
AIM_DEMO_MEMORIES receives semantic, episodic, and operational records. AIM_DEMO_TRACES receives three shareable outcomes.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:51.000
The library ranks only Ava's records, builds a context card, and returns zero Ava records for Leo.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:59.000
The Java path searches four durable record types, then combines ranked memory and recent messages into reusable context.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Oracle AI Database generates the query vector and ranks matching OAMJ_CONCIERGE_RECORDS while Ava's scope remains enforced.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:15.000
The deliberately imperfect fireworks fact remains visible so the next action can demonstrate correction.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Java reads only active, unexpired, visitor-and-agent-scoped rows and inserts one recall audit row per selected memory.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:31.000
AIM_DEMO_RECALL_AUDIT records the query, memory identifier, recall reason, visitor, and time for every selected row.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:38.000
The UI keeps the old version for audit and activates the guest-confirmed replacement.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Java locks the current fact, inserts version 2, updates version 1 to SUPERSEDED, and commits both changes atomically.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:54.000
AIM_DEMO_MEMORIES shows the old yellow SUPERSEDED row and the new green ACTIVE version 2 row with guest-correction provenance.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:01.000
The UI removes the temporary operational record from active recall while durable preferences remain.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Java updates rain-route-tonight from ACTIVE to EXPIRED and sets EXPIRES_AT to the database timestamp.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:16.000
AIM_DEMO_MEMORIES highlights the changed EXPIRED row. Future active-and-unexpired queries no longer select it.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:24.000
The app induces one pending rainy-evening-reroute candidate without copying Ava's private details.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Java counts matching episodes and inserts generalized JSON instructions with status PENDING.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:40.000
AIM_DEMO_SKILLS receives one green PENDING row with the trigger, generalized steps, source count, and no private guest data.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.000
The UI changes the induced skill from pending to approved and displays instructions that contain no Ava-specific facts.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Java records the approver and approval time while changing the status from PENDING to APPROVED.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:02.000
AIM_DEMO_SKILLS highlights the changed row with APPROVED status, APPROVED_BY, and APPROVED_AT.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:10.000
The app shows zero Ava memories visible to Leo and the approved rainy-evening-reroute behavior.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:18.000
Java proves that Ava rows under Leo's private scope equal zero, then selects only APPROVED shared skills.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:26.000
The final refresh reports zero added, changed, or removed rows. Leo reuses the lesson, not Ava's personal history.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:34.000
The park graph, spatial map, consented party, quest, and knowledge remain reusable while visitor-specific quest results return to zero.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:42.000
Java deletes badges, reward audit, and progress in foreign-key-safe order, then commits without rebuilding the park topology.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:50.000
AIM_PARK_PROGRESS, AIM_PARK_GUEST_BADGES, and AIM_PARK_REWARD_AUDIT show no rows; graph and knowledge tables remain populated.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:58.000
The map highlights a 675-meter accessible route and keeps the inaccessible Summit Steps visible. Spatial straight-line distance is 592 meters.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:06.000
Java filters closed or inaccessible graph relationships, finds the shortest permitted path, and asks Oracle Spatial for point-to-point distance.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:14.000
AIM_PARK_PATHS exposes directed connects edges with distance, accessibility, cover, and status used by AIM_PARK_GRAPH.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:22.000
The app activates three ordered checkpoints and records the quest start while points remain zero.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:30.000
One transaction creates Ava's active progress and the QUEST_STARTED audit event; party consent is read from member_of graph edges.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:38.000
AIM_PARK_PROGRESS shows step zero and ACTIVE status while AIM_PARK_REWARD_AUDIT records QUEST_STARTED with a zero-point delta.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:46.000
The verified UI shows three completed checkpoints, 400 audited points, the Lantern Pathfinder badge, and four reward events.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Java locks Ava's progress row, advances only the next ordered step, adds points, and issues the badge inside the final completion transaction.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Progress is COMPLETED with 400 points; the badge row and four audit events provide consistent, inspectable evidence.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:11.000
The app preserves cosine distance, connected places, and quest membership before presenting the grounded park answer.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Java embeds the request, ranks AIM_PARK_KNOWLEDGE, and follows connects and quest_step edges around every vector hit.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:28.000
AIM_PARK_KNOWLEDGE stores grounded content with 384-dimensional vectors; AIM_PARK_GRAPH supplies the connected place and quest structure.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Oracle AI Database keeps agent memory scoped and auditable, then combines graph, Spatial, vectors, and transactions for a safe playable experience.
